+## V2 minimal wall-cap successor
+
+This immutable source-only successor addresses the single B1 recorded in `pubmed_heart_native_numerical_fresh_source_review_20261004_v1/REVIEW.txt`. V1 and that review remain preserved. The runnable change is limited to `supervise.py`: prepare qualification/final-custody hash-and-size descriptors first, then sample final inclusive elapsed once immediately before completion classification. That same value controls final wall-cap refusal and `inclusive_supervisor_wall_seconds`. An overshoot cannot become COMPLETE; an existing earlier violation is preserved. CPU180s and real_graph3600s caps remain unchanged. Only terminal construction/final write/return work after that declared sample remains outside the measured boundary; the terminal final write tail remains explicitly unmeasured.
+
+`qualify.py`, `native_bodies.py`, `PLAN.json`, `SOURCE_BINDING.json` and both disabled templates are byte-identical to v1. Native recipes, numerical comparisons, schedule/work counts, stages, execution-root name, gate and later scientific stages are unchanged. The original STATIC_SOURCE_REVIEW is preserved in v1; v2 replaces that metadata with an honest source-only change record and does not inherit its compile assertions as checks of changed code.
+
+Exact predecessor/review pins, changed and identical payloads, and the unified diff are bound by PREDECESSOR_BINDING.json, SOURCE_CHANGE.json and the new manifest/seal. No proposed source was imported, AST-parsed, compiled, executed or staged. No SSH, data, model, checkpoint, TEST or outcomes were accessed. Root must obtain a fresh review and separately qualify the controlled below-cap/at-cap/over-cap boundary, including a wait4 sample below the cap followed by descriptor preparation that crosses it. No current source PASS, runtime qualification or execution release is asserted.
